    '</br></br>88. In the event that the closure is due to your account becoming an Inactive Account, UNObank shall notify you following the communication provision on Section 125 of this T&C and shall have the right to impose a one-time Inactivity Fee (refer to the UNObank website for the list of fees and charges), and remove the remaining funds in the Account and transfer the same to a liability account or such other account as UNObank may determine at its sole discretion, without prejudice to the turnover of the same to the Philippine treasury in accordance with the then applicable law, rules, and regulations.'
